Lumen 0.0.38 (04 Nov 2026)
==========================
Copyright (c) 2026 Andrew Youll. Released under the MIT licence: see
!Lumen.Licences.Lumen.

A photo library and non-destructive editor for RISC OS 5.
Lumen has importing, browsing, rating, flagging and albums;
captions, keywords and smart albums; versions and stacks; adjustments
(white balance with an eyedropper, exposure, highlights & shadows,
levels, curves, contrast, saturation, vibrancy, colour by hue, split
toning, noise reduction, sharpening, vignette, glow); Auto; crop, quarter
turns, straighten and perspective; grids; styles and presets; copying
adjustments between photos; exporting and printing; exporting,
importing and checking libraries.
Your photos are never changed: each edit is a recipe kept in the
library, and can be undone or reset at any time.

Getting started
---------------
Double-click !Lumen. Its window opens. Drag a folder of photos (JPEG,
PNG or TIFF) from the Filer onto the window or the icon bar icon. Lumen
reads them in the background and makes thumbnails; the desktop stays
usable while it works. Your photos are never changed or moved: the
library only refers to them. Photos are known by their first bytes, so
JPEG, PNG and TIFF files typed DOS, Text or Data, or with no extension,
are found too. TIFFs can be 8 or 16 bits a channel, compressed or not;
Lumen works on them at 8 bits.

The library lives in <Choices$Write>.Lumen.Library (normally inside
!Boot.Choices). To keep it elsewhere, set Lumen$Library before running
!Lumen, e.g.  *Set Lumen$Library SDFS::RISCOSpi.$.Photos.Library

